      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Katta Castrum [zone=470]\n**Who:**\n- Prime Researcher Elnot Waymun [npc=24719]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 70\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Loot\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Associate Researcher Plik [npc=24729]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Solteris Access #1: Knowledge for Power [quest=4051]\n- Solteris Access #1a: A City in Peril [quest=4106]\n- Solteris Access #2: Locating the Statue [quest=4052]\n- Solteris Access #2a: A City in Peril [quest=4107]\n- Solteris Access #2b: A City in Peril [quest=4108]\n- Solteris Access #3: Snakes Hiding Something [quest=4053]\n- Solteris Access #4: Counter-Attack! [quest=4054]\n- Solteris Access #4a: A City in Peril [quest=4109]\n- Solteris Access #5: Confront Emperor Vaakiszh [quest=4102]\n- Solteris Access #5a: A City in Peril - Make Contact with the Shissar Loyalists [quest=4438]\n- Solteris Access #6: Where There's a Will [quest=4103]\n- Solteris Access #7: Slay the Serpent [quest=4104]\n- Solteris Access #8: Stop the Ritual [quest=4105]\n- Solteris Access #8a: A City in Peril [quest=4110]\n**Era:** | !The Buried Sea\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sat Feb 17 15:00:38 2007\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | _Access to Solteris, the Throne of Ro, is granted after completing the following quest arc:_\nSolteris Access #0: A City in Peril\nSolteris Access #1: Knowledge of Power\nSolteris Access #1a: A City in Peril\nSolteris Access #2: Locating the Statue\nSolteris Access #2a: A City in Peril\nSolteris Access #2b: A City in Peril\nSolteris Access #3: The Snakes are Hiding Something!\nSolteris Access #4: Counter-Attack\nSolteris Access #5: Confront Emperor Zaarisz\nSolteris Access #5a: A City in Peril\nSolteris Access #6: Where There's a Will\nSolteris Access #7: Slay the Serpent\nSolteris Access #8: Stop the Ritual\nSolteris Access #8a: A City in Peril\n_The 'A City in Peril' tasks (\"mini-tasks\") listed here are obtained by speaking with Prime Researcher Elnot Waymun after completing missions #1, 2, 5, and 8. These usually involve only turn-ins or hailing certain NPC(s) and can be done by yourself, without the aid of a group._\n_These mini-tasks upgrade your Combine Signet Ring and allow you to request missions further along in the line of progression._\n\\\\*\\\\*\\\\*\\\\* NOTE: You must equip your ring in order for upgrades to take place.\n_As of 29 February 2008, Prime Researcher Elnot Waymun offers an additional prompt to help guide you..._\nYou say, 'Hail, Prime Researcher Elnot Waymun'\nPrime Researcher Elnot Waymun says 'If you have lost your way and need [guidance] let me know \\_\\_\\_\\_.'\n_Example..._\nYou say, 'guidance'\nPrime Researcher Elnot Waymun says 'You must return to Vizier Zio and Slay the Serpent.'\n_Subject to a couple of limitations, the group missions can be done out of order, providing someone in your group has enough faction to request the mission. Mission #6 and #7 and #8 require that you have completed #5, in order to have acccess to Silyssar. The teleports that you use in Mission #7 and #8 are unlocked in Mission #6.. although there are ways to bypass them._\n\n---\n\n_**Solteris Access #0: A City in Peril**_\nYou say, 'Hail, Prime Researcher Elnot Waymun'\nPrime Researcher Elnot Waymin says 'Good day to you \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Or as good as it can be in these [dark times].'\nYou say, 'Dark times?'\nPrime Researcher Elnot Waymun says 'Do you even need to ask? You should know better than I that the skies are darkening and there is a mystery even to the wise among us. The [grave peril] that our city finds itself in must be related to the dark skies but try as I might I cannot discover the link!\nYou say, 'Grave peril?'\nPrime Researcher Elnot Waymun says 'All you see around you is protected from the cold, dark sea above us by a single artifact atop the central tower that is known as the Pellarus Satum. It is this artifact that provides this protective dome of magic over our heads and in turn, through several smaller artifacts, safeguards other regions we used to oversee.' But now all of that is [failing]!\nYou say, 'How is it failing?'\nPrime Researcher Elnot Waymun says 'Every day the Pellarus Satuum grows [weaker]. At first it was only the faintest darkening, but now anyone can see that the light within has dimmed and with it he protective domes have begun to fail. I just received word that fissures in the magic have started to appear in the Zhisza! Can it be too long before Katta Castrum itself is swallowed by the seas as Prexus had intended!'\nYou say, 'Weaker?'\nPrime Researcher Elnot Waymun says 'No one knows why the Pellarus Satum is failing but we would not be the Combine if we did not have at least two theories being pursued! As you may know, our current location is due to a, uh, misunderstanding we had with Prexus. Some here believe that Prexus himself is the cause of our misfortune and has returned to finish his work. Our second theory is less refined. We don't know what is causing the Pellarus Satum to fail but we believe the Sphinx may hold the answer. That is the tack I wish to [pursue].\nYou say, 'Pursue?'\n_Receive Combine Signet Ring._\nYou have been assigned the task 'A City in Peril'.\n_There is only a single step for this task:_\nGo and speak with Associate Researcher Plik (Katta Castrum)\nYou say, 'Hail, Associate Researcher Plik'\nAssociate Researcher Plik says 'Ahh so Prime Resaercher Elnot sent you to speak with the sphinx about our [problem], yes?\n_This ends this task and leads into the first progression mission, \"Knowledge for Power\"._\n- Combine Signet Ring [item=64864]",
